<h1 class="hdg h1 hdg-cap ff-light hdg-blue">Eagan Wastewater Spill</h1>
    <div class="subhead">
        <div class="hdg h4 hdg-grey ff-medium"></div>
    </div>
</hgroup>
<div class='spill-description wysiwyg'>The Metropolitan Council, operator of the regional wastewater collection and treatment system, responded Tuesday afternoon, November 3, to a call from the City of Eagan reporting a wastewater spill. The spill occurred in Eagan, east of Lone Oak Circle and north of Lone Oak Road, along the Progressive Rail. The spill was caused by infrastructure failure. It was isolated and contained by Met Council crews in under an hour from the time of notice. No waterbodies were impacted by the spill.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Crews are onsite, have contained the spill, and are determining the scale of impact. Cleanup efforts and repairs are in process. Sewer service will not be interrupted.<br />
<br />
An update will be provided as we learn more.   &nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;</div>

<div class="wysiwyg" >
  
<div class="ec_wrapper ec_compact ec_default_open">
